{"tool_name":"genskew","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"genskew","home":"http://genskew.csb.univie.ac.at/","summary":"G+C skew plot of microbial genomes.","addition_date":"2015-11-05T14:34:20Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-16T14:26:03Z","tool_type":["Desktop application","Web application"],"version":["1"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:genskew","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"m.muensterkoetter@uni-sopron.hu","name":"Martin M\u00fcnsterk\u00f6tter","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0044-2381","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"contact.cube@univie.ac.at","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"AT-CUBE","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://genskew.csb.univie.ac.at/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"DNA sequence (raw)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3497"}}],"note":"Nucleotide skew plot oriC and ter coordinates","operation":[{"term":"Genome visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3208"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Image","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2968"}},{"data":{"term":"Sequence features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1255"}}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"GenSkew","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"AT-CUBE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkj148","metadata":{"abstract":"The Munich Information Center for Protein Sequences (MIPS at the GSF), Neuherberg, Germany, provides resources related to genome information. Manually curated databases for several reference organisms are maintained. Several of these databases are described elsewhere in this and other recent NAR database issues. In a complementary effort, a comprehensive set of >400 genomes automatically annotated with the PEDANT system are maintained. The main goal of our current work on creating and maintaining genome databases is to extend gene centered information to information on interactions within a generic comprehensive framework. We have concentrated our efforts along three lines (i) the development of suitable comprehensive data structures and database technology, communication and query tools to include a wide range of different types of information enabling the representation of complex information such as functional modules or networks Genome Research Environment System, (ii) the development of databases covering computable information such as the basic evolutionary relations among all genes, namely SIMAP, the sequence similarity matrix and the CABiNet network analysis framework and (iii) the compilation and manual annotation of information related to interactions such as protein-protein interactions or other types of relations (e.g. MPCDB, MPPI, CYGD). All databases described and the detailed descriptions of our projects can be accessed through the MIPS WWW server (http://mips.gsf.de).","authors":[{"name":"Frishman D."},{"name":"Mayer K.F."},{"name":"Mewes H.W."},{"name":"Munsterkotter M."},{"name":"Noubibou O."},{"name":"Oesterheld M."},{"name":"Pagel P."},{"name":"Rattei T."},{"name":"Ruepp A."},{"name":"Stumpflen V."}],"citationCount":292,"date":"2006-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic acids research","title":"MIPS: analysis and annotation of proteins from whole genomes in 2005."},"pmcid":"PMC1347510","pmid":"16381839","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"GenSkew","home":"https://bio.tools/genskew","version":"1","summary":"G+C skew plot of microbial genomes.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:genskew:1/app/genskew.csb.univie.ac.at","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation